Omnispeak @VERSION@ for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
=================================================================

Omnispeak is an open-source engine for Commander Keen 4, 5 and 6 ("Goodbye
Galaxy" and "Aliens Ate My Baby Sitter"). This is its AmigaOS 3.x build for
a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, on acsdl12 (SDL 1.2 over ACGame and AHI).
Status: TESTING, not a release.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.x, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, AGA or an RTG board.
- AHI for sound.
- The Keen game data (not in this archive): see Data-ReadMe.txt.

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive where you keep games (lha x omnispeak-...lha Games:),
then copy the Keen data files into the Keen drawer itself. Settings and
saves are written there too.

Playing
-------

- Double-click the omnispeak icon, or from a Shell: cd to the drawer, then
  omnispeak. It plays the episode whose data it finds; with more than one,
  /EPISODE 4, /EPISODE 5 or /EPISODE 6 picks it.
- ENV:ACGame/Display set to AGA or RTG chooses the screen.
- Keys: the arrow keys move, Ctrl jumps, Alt pogos, Space fires, Escape
  opens the menu.

Licence
-------

Omnispeak is GPL-2.0 (LICENSE.txt); its source is at
https://github.com/sulix/omnispeak. The Keen data belongs to its makers and
is not part of this archive. The icons are drawn from Omnispeak's own
program icon.

